      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "edge-smoketest"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='position:relative;width:2560px;height:1060px;background:#f8fafc;color:#0f172a;overflow:hidden;font-family:system-ui'><div style='position:absolute;left:50px;top:36px;font:700 14px system-ui;letter-spacing:0.16em;color:#6d28d9'>EDGES · SMOKE TEST</div><div style='position:absolute;left:50px;top:62px;font:400 38px Georgia,serif'>Edge smoke test</div><div style='position:absolute;left:50px;top:118px;width:1500px;font:400 17px/1.5 system-ui;color:#475569'>Edge names and travel along edges.<br><b>Inside this graph:</b> click an edge’s <i>stroke</i> to frame it, select it, then travel to its far end. Click an edge’s <i>name</i> to go to the edge’s own graph.<br>“described by a graph” leads to a graph about that edge. “has a class page” leads to the Link class page. “just an edge” leads nowhere, so a click on its name is a click on the edge.<br><b>Between graphs:</b> double-click the two Portals on the right, then step out (Escape) to the workspace. Each trunk’s stroke carries a small name: click the stroke to frame, select and travel; click the name to go to the Portal class page.<br>The link in the last node makes a third kind of stroke, a Link.</div></div>"
        }
      },
      "positionLocked": true
    },
